1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,587
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:06,673
[gunshots]

3
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:07,966
[gun clicks, fires]

4
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,677
[whoosh, slashing sounds]

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,679
[machine gun fire]

6
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:14,681
[machine gun fire continues]

7
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:15,765
[single gunshot]

8
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:20,395
[rapid gunfire]

9
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,397
[echoing blast]

10
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,107
[rapid gunfire]

11
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:25,942
[blade whooshing]

12
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,445
[tense music builds]

13
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,696
[blade whooshing]

14
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:34,743
[Marlon] <i>Friends, gather all</i>
<i>the citizens of Ardiente.</i>

15
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:36,494
<i>Even the Ardiente loyalists.</i>

16
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:39,414
<i>Call the press so the whole world</i>

17
00:00:39,497 --> 00:00:40,749
<i>can see the ruthlessness of the Ardientes.</i>

18
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:43,376
[woman] <i>Justice for the</i>
<i>victims of the Ardientes!</i>

19
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:44,753
[man] <i>It's time for retribution.</i>

20
00:00:44,836 --> 00:00:46,129
<i>Down with the Ardientes!</i>

21
00:00:46,212 --> 00:00:49,466
<i>Thank you for gathering</i>
<i>the townspeople today.</i>

22
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:53,845
<i>Now they can see just how</i>
<i>tainted your souls really are!</i>

23
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:55,138
<i>Arrest them! Arrest them all!</i>

24
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:56,765
-[gunshots and screams]
<i>-Papa!</i>

25
00:00:57,849 --> 00:01:01,061
[Julio] <i>You ruined Ardiente.</i>

26
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:02,437
<i>This is your fault!</i>

27
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,938
[chair clatters]

28
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,692
-<i>Lily! Lily!</i>
-[crowd] <i>Long live!</i>

29
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:12,489
[cheers and applause]

30
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:15,033
[Julio] <i>Secure the perimeter.</i>

31
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,327
<i>I don't want any intruders in this house.</i>

32
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:19,412
<i>I'm sorry to say this,</i>
<i>but we've lost many of our men.</i>

33
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:21,372
<i>Most have surrendered, and many are hurt.</i>

34
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:23,124
[Julio] <i>I don't give a damn!</i>

35
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,752
<i>No one comes into my fortress.</i>

36
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,796
<i>Because this house is unsinkable.</i>

37
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:30,757
<i>I am unsinkable!</i>

38
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:32,050
[Sanggano] <i>Men, stand down!</i>

39
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:33,259
<i>-Governor!</i>
<i>-Colonel!</i>

40
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:35,136
<i>Get inside! Please!</i>

41
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,222
[Emilia] <i>Enough, Papa. Enough!</i>

42
00:01:37,305 --> 00:01:38,348
<i>We have to go!</i>

43
00:01:38,431 --> 00:01:40,558
<i>The whole house is surrounded!</i>

44
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:41,768
[Julio] <i>Pigs!</i>

45
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:44,020
<i>Pathetic ingrates!</i>

46
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:54,697
[crowd clamoring]

47
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:57,283
Ooh. [chuckles]

48
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:59,369
Now, this…

49
00:01:59,452 --> 00:02:02,705
This is revenge.

50
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:05,583
And it tastes so sweet.

51
00:02:06,126 --> 00:02:07,919
I never tasted revenge like this.

52
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:10,380
It tastes so delicious.

53
00:02:10,463 --> 00:02:12,132
It actually tastes like honey.

54
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:15,135
But

55
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:19,889
I must apologize to everyone
for being fashionably late.

56
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:24,269
Because I was dealing with my emotions.

57
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:25,812
My loneliness.

58
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:29,023
With Arnaldo…

59
00:02:29,107 --> 00:02:32,318
Then, Raul…

60
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:34,904
And now, Madrigal.

61
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:36,322
But

62
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:37,824
I'm back.

63
00:02:39,617 --> 00:02:43,121
And I guess it's better late
than never, right?

64
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:44,622
[chuckles]

65
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:48,918
I wish I was as cutthroat as Lily Cruz.

66
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:53,756
For some reason, she makes revenge look so

67
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:56,885
fashionable and possible.

68
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:05,310
But this is exactly what I want.

69
00:03:05,393 --> 00:03:07,061
This is perfect.

70
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:12,108
Angelo, take me to the back.

71
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:18,364
And I'll give the Ardientes
a little surprise.

72
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:20,116
Yes, Lady N.

73
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:21,576
[chuckles]

74
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:25,413
[engine rumbles]

75
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:26,873
[Emilia] Let's go, Papa.

76
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:40,011
[Natalie] What's the rush, evil witch?

77
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,056
Natalie?

78
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:45,266
You, crazy witch!

79
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:49,270
And what the hell are you doing here, huh?

80
00:03:49,979 --> 00:03:51,981
We already have our plate full
at the mansion.

81
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:53,358
We don't have time for you.

82
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:54,317
I know!

83
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,903
I saw, and that's why I'm here.

84
00:03:56,986 --> 00:03:58,947
I want to enjoy this moment.

85
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:01,115
Poor Emilia.

86
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:02,867
Poor Ardientes.

87
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:05,328
I was thinking to myself,

88
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:07,914
what were you both thinking, huh?

89
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:12,126
After all the mortal sins
that you and your family did?

90
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:15,046
Your daughter killed my father!

91
00:04:15,129 --> 00:04:16,714
Hey! And look who's talking, huh?

92
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:19,509
Wasn't cheating with my husband
revenge enough for you?

93
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:22,637
You killed your own husband!

94
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,055
You murderer!

95
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:28,309
Emilia, just cut the drama
and kill her already!

96
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:29,811
Go back there, Papa!

97
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:33,564
You crazy woman!

98
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:34,941
Come on!

99
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:36,985
Isn't this what you wanted?!

100
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:40,280
You wanted us to kill each other!

101
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:42,031
-You witch… [screams]
-[gunshot]

102
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:44,742
What are you doing?

103
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:48,538
Everyone, guess who's here!

104
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:50,039
The Ardientes!

105
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:52,208
-You crazy witch!
-They're here!

106
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,669
-Shoot!
-The Ardientes are here!

107
00:04:54,752 --> 00:04:56,879
-[Emilia] This--
-Hey, guys!

108
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:59,048
Come here, everyone!

109
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:01,134
Over here, everyone!

110
00:05:01,217 --> 00:05:03,761
-There they are!
-Hurry!

111
00:05:17,608 --> 00:05:20,403
<i>That serves you right, you evil witch!</i>

112
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:22,447
<i>Do what you cowards do best,</i>

113
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:26,117
<i>other than stabbing people</i>
<i>on their backs literally.</i>

114
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:28,870
<i>Run, run as fast as you can.</i>

115
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:31,080
<i>And don't even dare coming back!</i>

116
00:05:32,123 --> 00:05:35,626
<i>Daddy, I know you're proud</i>
<i>of your little girl.</i>

117
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:38,254
<i>Justice has been served.</i>

118
00:05:38,337 --> 00:05:40,506
<i>And it tastes so delicious.</i>

119
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:41,841
<i>I love you, Daddy.</i>

120
00:05:42,216 --> 00:05:44,719
[tense music playing]

121
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:48,765
This can't be happening, Papa.

122
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:50,641
This can't be happening.

123
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,852
In the blink of an eye,
we lost our fortune,

124
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:55,188
our power, and our province.

125
00:05:55,271 --> 00:05:56,731
What are we going to do now?

126
00:05:58,691 --> 00:06:01,235
We are not leaving Poblacion Ardiente.

127
00:06:02,278 --> 00:06:03,780
I built this town.

128
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:06,032
I <i>own</i> this town.

129
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:08,868
I am this town!

130
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:13,581
Papa, this province destroyed us.

131
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:17,085
The people here no longer want us!

132
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:19,128
Where do we go now?

133
00:06:19,212 --> 00:06:21,339
Oh, shut up, Emilia!

134
00:06:21,422 --> 00:06:23,341
Don't think I've forgotten.

135
00:06:24,008 --> 00:06:26,552
It was your actions that brought

136
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:28,971
Lily Cruz into our lives.

137
00:06:29,514 --> 00:06:30,598
Now, look.

138
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:33,309
See how the mighty have fallen.

139
00:06:33,392 --> 00:06:36,979
This is because of the
useless women in my life.

140
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:39,690
I'm the father of this town.

141
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,943
I gave them everything.

142
00:06:42,026 --> 00:06:44,028
I gave them Poblacion Ardiente.

143
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:45,655
And this is how they repay me?

144
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:47,907
By storming my mansion like a plague!

145
00:06:48,157 --> 00:06:51,786
What a bunch of lowlife ingrates!

146
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:54,997
We will not leave this town.

147
00:06:55,706 --> 00:07:02,755
I will never let a woman
and a bastard take my place!

148
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:06,050
No.

149
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:09,178
I will not accept defeat!

150
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:12,765
Stop the car. Stop it right now!

151
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:14,267
-What?
-Stop it!

152
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:18,020
[tires screech]

153
00:07:18,938 --> 00:07:20,189
[car door opens]

154
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:21,399
[handbrake clicks]

155
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:24,610
[ominous music playing]

156
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:42,044
I never thought it would come to this.

157
00:07:44,088 --> 00:07:46,841
That a single wildflower…

158
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:51,929
would take down a king like me.

159
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:56,934
We created the monster
of our own destruction, Papa.

160
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:00,688
And that monster is that witch, Lily Cruz.

161
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:05,026
Born from your jealousy.

162
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:09,030
You had Dante Cruz killed…

163
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:12,158
to stop him from investigating.

164
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,661
You were just trying to protect

165
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:18,372
my name and our family.

166
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:21,083
And in the process…

167
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:26,964
you also protected the people
of Poblacion Ardiente.

168
00:08:29,509 --> 00:08:30,801
But Papa,

169
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:35,056
the people who loved us before
will never forgive us again.

170
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:38,518
It's over, Papa. We have
nothing to come back to.

171
00:08:40,436 --> 00:08:42,939
Forgiveness is overrated.

172
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:48,736
What matters most is fear.

173
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:54,617
Sadly, they do not fear us anymore.

174
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:57,411
[ominous music continues]

175
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:03,334
I shed blood, sweat, and tears

176
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:07,797
to establish Poblacion Ardiente.

177
00:09:09,423 --> 00:09:10,424
So…

178
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:14,679
Blood, sweat, and tears will spill

179
00:09:15,429 --> 00:09:17,390
over the land they took from me.

180
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:20,434
[ominous music playing]

181
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:29,318
WELCOME TO POBLACION ARDIENTE

182
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:43,457
[car door closes]

183
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,209
[engine starts]

184
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:50,089
[car door closes]

185
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:55,469
[ominous music continues]

186
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:13,821
[bright music playing]

187
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,424
[Lily] <i>With every smile they show…</i>

188
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:41,223
<i>with every hug and</i>
<i>expression of gratitude…</i>

189
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:45,311
<i>I'm reminded of the reason</i>
<i>why I kept fighting.</i>

190
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:50,816
<i>So that there will never be</i>

191
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,194
<i>victims of abuse and violence again.</i>

192
00:10:53,819 --> 00:10:59,367
<i>No more shattered dreams</i>
<i>and victims of injustice.</i>

193
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:02,662
<i>No more broken families.</i>

194
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:05,414
[uplifting music playing]

195
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:09,126
[crowd cheering]

196
00:11:11,003 --> 00:11:17,051
<i>I kept fighting for those who</i>
<i>dreamt of freedom and change.</i>

197
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:21,931
<i>I kept fighting so no one</i>
<i>will ever have to experience</i>

198
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:24,350
<i>the suffering I went through.</i>

199
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:26,936
[cheers and indistinct chatter]

200
00:11:27,853 --> 00:11:33,359
<i>If this is the reward for</i>
<i>everything we went through,</i>

201
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,028
<i>then it was worth it.</i>

202
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:39,740
[crowd chanting] Diego! Diego! Diego!

203
00:11:46,705 --> 00:11:48,165
[chanting continues]

204
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:53,879
[Georgina] Camia, the witnesses are here.

205
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:56,173
They're ready to support Lily and Diego.

206
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:57,758
Thank you, Attorney.

207
00:11:58,717 --> 00:11:59,760
Arthur?

208
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:01,303
Arthur.

209
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:07,268
Where are you going?

210
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:13,274
I'm leaving this place.

211
00:12:14,984 --> 00:12:18,404
The scars that the Ardientes
inflicted on me are too deep.

212
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:22,450
I don't think I can
still go on living here.

213
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:26,328
That's why we're here.

214
00:12:27,204 --> 00:12:28,664
So we can help you.

215
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:29,999
[sighs]

216
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:32,877
You've already done enough.

217
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:39,091
The kindness you've shown me
is already enough.

218
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:41,343
But your trust…

219
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:45,181
The trust that you and Lily have given me…

220
00:12:45,264 --> 00:12:51,187
A person like me doesn't deserve that
after everything I did to you.

221
00:12:52,396 --> 00:12:54,732
After I ruined both of your lives.

222
00:12:57,526 --> 00:12:59,069
Arthur, you were a victim too.

223
00:13:00,237 --> 00:13:02,656
We were all victims of the Ardientes.

224
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,453
I did what I did because I was a coward.

225
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:10,372
And, I think, if I stay here,

226
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:14,168
I'll forever be haunted by my conscience.

227
00:13:15,419 --> 00:13:17,213
What's done is done.

228
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:20,508
What's important is that no more lives

229
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:23,093
will be ruined because of them.

230
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:27,890
And it's all because of your help

231
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:30,851
and your courage.

232
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:36,148
We'll be waiting for you to return, okay?

233
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:38,984
[solemn music playing]

234
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:48,160
If you ever need me,

235
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:50,871
you know how to reach me.

236
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:56,919
Take care of yourself.

237
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:18,274
[unsettling music playing]

238
00:14:26,490 --> 00:14:27,491
[suppressed gunshot]

239
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:33,122
Camia.

240
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,501
Forgive me.

241
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,379
Please forgive me, Camia.

242
00:14:40,462 --> 00:14:42,840
[unsettling music continues]

243
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,843
I'm ready to face…

244
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:48,596
the punishment I deserve
for what I did to you.

245
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:52,349
Just grant me one favor.

246
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:55,477
Please forgive me.

247
00:15:00,649 --> 00:15:03,611
What you're asking for
can't be given that easily.

248
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:06,530
[tense music playing]

249
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:10,534
You were deaf to my screams and pleas

250
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:12,369
when you were molesting me.

251
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:15,956
And when you tried to kill me.

252
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:20,920
Whatever punishment you expect
will never be enough

253
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:23,505
for the horror you put me through.

254
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:29,219
But…

255
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:34,308
But right now, I'm exhausted.

256
00:15:34,391 --> 00:15:36,727
[tense music continues]

257
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:40,230
Exhausted from carrying the burden

258
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:42,858
of all the hardships I've gone through.

259
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:47,279
I used to think that…

260
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:51,200
I would never be reunited
with my daughter again.

261
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:55,621
I thought

262
00:15:56,455 --> 00:16:00,000
that I would never get justice
for my husband's death.

263
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,337
And I thought

264
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:06,298
this town would never be
free of the Ardientes.

265
00:16:08,133 --> 00:16:10,052
But now, I know…

266
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,430
that anything is possible.

267
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:17,685
As long as you have unwavering courage

268
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:20,354
and love in your heart.

269
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:26,694
I was able to forget
about Raul and what he did.

270
00:16:29,154 --> 00:16:30,364
So, Tonio…

271
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:36,662
In time, I'll be able to
forgive you for what you did.

272
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:40,916
[breathes heavily]

273
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:44,461
Thank you, Camia.

274
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:46,922
Thank you very much.

275
00:16:47,214 --> 00:16:49,633
[uplifting music playing]

276
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:59,852
[soft music playing]

277
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:08,694
Mom.

278
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:13,115
[chuckles]

279
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:15,117
This is it.

280
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:22,291
Our fight against the
Ardientes is almost over.

281
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,752
We took back power

282
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:26,920
and gave it to the people.

283
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:28,881
That's why we're free now, Mom.

284
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:32,301
You're right, dear.

285
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:35,137
But as long as Julio and Emilia

286
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:36,638
continue to roam free,

287
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:42,269
the justice we fought to seek
won't truly be served.

288
00:17:42,644 --> 00:17:45,272
[soft music continues]

289
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:50,402
We're almost there, Mom.

290
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:53,030
We've come a long way.

291
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:59,203
I remember what Miss Prianka told me.

292
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:04,166
Seeking justice involves
a lot of patience.

293
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:06,960
And remember what Dad always used to say?

294
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:12,800
Fight, hope, and change.

295
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:20,557
<i>And how change could only</i>
<i>be achieved through love.</i>

296
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,726
<i>Love for oneself,</i>

297
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:26,939
<i>love for others, and love for our nation.</i>

298
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:31,777
For this town.

299
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:33,403
Lily.

300
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:36,615
I do hope this is the end…

301
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:41,370
and not the beginning
of an even bigger battle.

302
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:43,705
[soft music playing]

303
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:47,709
This is the end, Mom.

304
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:49,920
I'll make sure of it.

305
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:53,924
The Ardientes won't
just lose their mansion.

306
00:18:54,007 --> 00:18:55,467
If they come back,

307
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:58,470
I'll make sure to take
everything they have,

308
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:03,851
so they can pay for all their crimes.

309
00:19:09,064 --> 00:19:10,899
[reporter] <i>Where are Julio Ardiente</i>

310
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:12,693
and Emilia Ardiente-Torillo hiding?

311
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:14,736
Until now, the authorities
are still searching

312
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:17,156
for the two Ardientes.

313
00:19:17,614 --> 00:19:18,949
<i>Meanwhile, the position of…</i>

314
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:21,243
The Ardientes have been defeated.

315
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:23,036
[reporter] <i>Julio Ardiente fled</i>

316
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:25,455
<i>when the people revolted against him.</i>

317
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:28,041
<i>And since Vice Governor Mateo Ruiz</i>

318
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,627
<i>is in hiding for being</i>
<i>associated with a syndicate,</i>

319
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:34,631
<i>the provincial board member</i>
<i>with the most votes</i>

320
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,216
<i>will replace Julio Ardiente.</i>

321
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,593
<i>But the people want Diego Torillo,</i>

322
00:19:37,676 --> 00:19:42,472
<i>Julio Ardiente's past election</i>
<i>rival, to be their governor.</i>

323
00:19:46,226 --> 00:19:48,520
[woman] I'm sorry, Lily. I didn't know.

324
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:50,439
I'm sorry for what I did.

325
00:19:50,814 --> 00:19:52,566
That's all in the past.

326
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:54,610
[Edna] Miss Lily.

327
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,236
Governor.

328
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:57,571
Edna.

329
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:00,532
[Ronald] It's the governor.

330
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:01,658
Ma'am.

331
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:03,660
[Diego] How are you?

332
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:04,995
[Ronald] We're good, we're good.

333
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:07,372
Thank you.

334
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:10,792
At last, our parents are finally at peace.

335
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,128
[Ronald] Thanks to you,

336
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:16,089
we finally got the justice
we used to only dream about.

337
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:19,218
We all have the same wish…

338
00:20:19,968 --> 00:20:22,804
because we've all been victims.

339
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:25,557
Our families were victims.

340
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:27,559
But you never backed down.

341
00:20:28,101 --> 00:20:29,603
You never gave up the fight.

342
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:31,688
You and Diego taught us

343
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:34,942
to never be silenced
and to fight for what's right.

344
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:38,570
Because of that, we thank you
with all our hearts.

345
00:20:38,987 --> 00:20:41,114
Even though the fight is over,

346
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:44,243
we hope you'll help us rebuild this town

347
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:46,119
so we can claim the hope

348
00:20:46,203 --> 00:20:48,747
that our people
have been long searching for.

349
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,332
[Efren] Governor.

350
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:52,501
We're ready to help you with that.

351
00:20:52,751 --> 00:20:55,379
You can count on us to be here for you.

352
00:20:56,004 --> 00:20:57,339
Thank you.

353
00:20:57,422 --> 00:20:58,674
Thank you, everyone.

354
00:20:58,757 --> 00:21:00,926
Thank you for supporting my husband.

355
00:21:01,551 --> 00:21:05,222
[tender music playing]

356
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:13,063
Whoa. I'm sorry--

357
00:21:15,482 --> 00:21:16,441
Anna.

358
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:17,526
Jepoy.

359
00:21:21,321 --> 00:21:23,949
The day we've been waiting for
finally arrived, huh?

360
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:30,205
I'm happy because we finally got

361
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:34,876
our long-awaited justice
against the Ardientes.

362
00:21:43,927 --> 00:21:45,137
Thank you, Anna.

363
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,556
Thank you so much.

364
00:21:53,603 --> 00:21:54,730
Really, thank you.

365
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:56,982
[ominous music playing]

366
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:03,572
[clears throat]

367
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:07,034
-Sorry to disturb your…
-[Jepoy] Natalie.

368
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,535
…platonic hug.

369
00:22:08,618 --> 00:22:10,787
I just wanted to say thank you

370
00:22:10,871 --> 00:22:13,040
because you knocked some sense into me.

371
00:22:13,999 --> 00:22:15,792
And you still believed that

372
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:18,587
I have a little goodness
in my indigo heart.

373
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:24,926
Thanks to you, Lily Cruz,
and the rest of the gang,

374
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:28,263
the evil Ardientes are now
evicted out of this town.

375
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:32,976
But, you and I…

376
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:37,105
We still have unfinished business.

377
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:38,940
Natalie.

378
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:41,443
Anna's the one I love.

379
00:22:44,613 --> 00:22:46,114
I've heard that before.

380
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:47,324
[chuckles]

381
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:49,117
Blah, blah, blah!

382
00:22:49,993 --> 00:22:53,872
We all seem to want what we can't have.

383
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:57,626
Am I right, Mr. Madrigal?

384
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:01,004
[Natalie] Ouch!

385
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:02,964
[sighs]

386
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:06,134
Little Miss Anna…

387
00:23:06,885 --> 00:23:08,178
Cherish it while it lasts,

388
00:23:08,261 --> 00:23:10,180
-because tomorrow…
-Natalie.

389
00:23:10,972 --> 00:23:12,349
…I'll be coming for him.

390
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,938
[tense music playing]

391
00:23:29,116 --> 00:23:30,117
Anna…

392
00:23:32,119 --> 00:23:33,537
[Jepoy] Anna, where are you going? Wait.

393
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:35,413
I'll be heading inside.

394
00:23:35,497 --> 00:23:36,957
-I'll go with you.
-I'll go with you.

395
00:23:38,875 --> 00:23:40,335
-I'll do it.
-I'll do it.

396
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:42,087
[Jepoy] No, I'll do it.

397
00:23:42,587 --> 00:23:43,672
I said I'll do it.

398
00:23:43,755 --> 00:23:45,507
I can manage. You two stay here.

399
00:23:47,008 --> 00:23:48,510
-Anna!
-[Jepoy mumbling]

400
00:23:49,594 --> 00:23:51,012
Are you hitting on Anna?

401
00:23:52,764 --> 00:23:55,475
-What do you think?
-I think you are.

402
00:23:55,559 --> 00:23:56,476
[sighs]

403
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:57,978
So what if I am?

404
00:23:59,062 --> 00:24:00,647
Just don't hurt her.

405
00:24:01,815 --> 00:24:04,985
Don't worry. I'm not like you.

406
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,363
Commissioner?

407
00:24:09,906 --> 00:24:13,243
Excuse me. Can I talk to the commissioner?

408
00:24:16,121 --> 00:24:17,956
Look at their smiles.

409
00:24:19,207 --> 00:24:21,001
They're all beaming.

410
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:25,463
That means that their dreams
finally came true.

411
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:29,759
That's why I ask you
to never allow the Ardientes

412
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:32,262
to take their dreams away.

413
00:24:33,972 --> 00:24:35,140
Don't worry.

414
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:39,352
We will give the people
what they truly deserve.

415
00:24:39,436 --> 00:24:42,189
[uplifting music playing]

416
00:24:49,613 --> 00:24:52,115
[cheers and applause]

417
00:24:56,494 --> 00:24:58,038
THE NEW ARDIENTE

418
00:24:58,121 --> 00:24:59,414
DIEGO, THE REAL GOVERNOR

419
00:25:07,005 --> 00:25:10,467
We've all gathered here today

420
00:25:10,550 --> 00:25:14,054
to let each and every one of you
know the truth.

421
00:25:16,014 --> 00:25:19,351
I'm ready to expose Julio Ardiente's lies

422
00:25:19,434 --> 00:25:21,228
during the last election.

423
00:25:21,311 --> 00:25:24,731
He paid me to manipulate the votes

424
00:25:24,814 --> 00:25:26,691
so that he would win.

425
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:29,861
But the truth is,

426
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:32,239
the real winner was none
other than Diego Torillo.

427
00:25:32,322 --> 00:25:34,407
[cheers and applause]

428
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:36,952
[bright music playing]

429
00:25:47,754 --> 00:25:52,133
We will make an appeal to the court
to recount the votes

430
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:56,137
so that we can finally have

431
00:25:56,221 --> 00:26:00,141
our town's true and rightful governor,

432
00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:01,893
Diego Torillo!

433
00:26:01,977 --> 00:26:03,645
[cheering, applause]

434
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:08,566
Diego is our governor!

435
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:10,193
Diego is the people's governor!

436
00:26:10,277 --> 00:26:12,904
[crowd chants] Diego! Diego! Diego!

437
00:26:12,988 --> 00:26:16,408
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

438
00:26:16,491 --> 00:26:19,953
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

439
00:26:20,036 --> 00:26:23,248
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

440
00:26:23,331 --> 00:26:25,792
[cheering and applause]

441
00:26:27,127 --> 00:26:31,006
It's been months
since we finally got rid of

442
00:26:31,089 --> 00:26:34,342
the people responsible
for destroying our town.

443
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:37,137
We can finally take back the power

444
00:26:37,220 --> 00:26:39,472
that should've never belonged to them.

445
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:44,019
We will wipe away all
the filth left in our town.

446
00:26:44,519 --> 00:26:46,896
Then, we will create together…

447
00:26:47,772 --> 00:26:49,858
a new Poblacion Ardiente!

448
00:26:50,275 --> 00:26:52,444
For the new Ardiente!

449
00:26:52,527 --> 00:26:54,696
[crowd] For the new Ardiente!

450
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:57,866
[crowd chants] Diego! Diego! Diego!

451
00:26:57,949 --> 00:27:00,535
-[uplifting music playing]
-[chanting continues]

452
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:10,170
[Lily] <i>Thank you, Miss Prianka,</i>

453
00:27:10,253 --> 00:27:13,715
<i>for making Ivy Aguas a part of my life.</i>

454
00:27:17,969 --> 00:27:21,890
<i>The Ivy Aguas who is ready</i>
<i>to fight for what is right.</i>

455
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:25,894
<i>The Ivy Aguas who never gives up</i>

456
00:27:25,977 --> 00:27:28,229
<i>no matter what life throws at her.</i>

457
00:27:28,605 --> 00:27:30,357
<i>But most of all,</i>

458
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:33,651
<i>the Ivy Aguas who taught Lily Cruz</i>

459
00:27:33,735 --> 00:27:35,445
<i>to be strong…</i>

460
00:27:35,904 --> 00:27:37,697
<i>fierce, and powerful.</i>

461
00:27:39,115 --> 00:27:41,451
<i>If it wasn't for you, Miss Prianka,</i>

462
00:27:41,534 --> 00:27:45,121
<i>there wouldn't be</i>
<i>an Ivy Aguas or a Lily Cruz.</i>

463
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:49,751
<i>She wouldn't have been able to teach</i>

464
00:27:49,834 --> 00:27:51,711
<i>the people of this town…</i>

465
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:54,756
<i>to go against the Ardientes.</i>

466
00:27:57,842 --> 00:27:59,552
<i>Like how you taught me</i>

467
00:27:59,636 --> 00:28:01,930
<i>to live my life with</i>
<i>righteousness in my heart.</i>

468
00:28:02,013 --> 00:28:04,682
[crowd chants] Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

469
00:28:04,766 --> 00:28:06,351
[chanting continues]

470
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:10,230
[Diego] <i>Nanny Loring, Uncle Pandoy…</i>

471
00:28:12,816 --> 00:28:15,652
<i>I'm sure you're both happy now</i>

472
00:28:15,735 --> 00:28:17,654
<i>that our fight is finally over.</i>

473
00:28:18,113 --> 00:28:19,656
<i>We won.</i>

474
00:28:19,739 --> 00:28:22,534
[uplifting music playing]

475
00:28:22,617 --> 00:28:26,704
<i>Thank you for raising and guiding me.</i>

476
00:28:26,996 --> 00:28:28,957
<i>If it wasn't for you both,</i>

477
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:31,459
<i>I wouldn't be who I am.</i>

478
00:28:31,543 --> 00:28:35,588
<i>A man ready to fight for what is right.</i>

479
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:38,425
[uplifting music continues]

480
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:46,975
<i>Dad…</i>

481
00:28:48,935 --> 00:28:52,063
<i>Thank you for always believing in me</i>

482
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:55,108
<i>as your son and as a man.</i>

483
00:28:56,151 --> 00:29:00,321
<i>Despite everything we endured</i>
<i>because of the Ardientes,</i>

484
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:02,866
<i>you were still a good father to me.</i>

485
00:29:02,949 --> 00:29:05,076
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

486
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:09,330
<i>And to everyone who sacrificed their lives</i>

487
00:29:09,414 --> 00:29:11,332
<i>for this day to come.</i>

488
00:29:20,675 --> 00:29:22,385
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

489
00:29:23,303 --> 00:29:25,054
<i>I promise…</i>

490
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:29,100
<i>that no blood will be spilled</i>
<i>in this town ever again.</i>

491
00:29:29,476 --> 00:29:31,936
[uplifting music playing]

492
00:29:36,941 --> 00:29:39,527
Thank you for all the times you saved me.

493
00:29:40,570 --> 00:29:42,322
I didn't save you alone.

494
00:29:43,114 --> 00:29:45,450
The townspeople were with me too.

495
00:29:45,533 --> 00:29:46,743
It's their way of thanking you

496
00:29:46,826 --> 00:29:48,828
for all the sacrifices
you've made for them.

497
00:29:48,912 --> 00:29:51,122
For defending them from all the cruelty

498
00:29:51,206 --> 00:29:55,210
they suffered at the hands
of the Ardientes.

499
00:29:59,088 --> 00:30:01,174
[cheers and applause]

500
00:30:12,101 --> 00:30:14,354
We'll make our dreams come true.

501
00:30:14,979 --> 00:30:16,064
You and me…

502
00:30:17,148 --> 00:30:20,568
we'll rebuild Poblacion Ardiente.

503
00:30:20,944 --> 00:30:22,779
You are my life, Diego.

504
00:30:25,740 --> 00:30:27,325
You are my governor.

505
00:30:29,953 --> 00:30:32,413
You are the governor of this province.

506
00:30:33,998 --> 00:30:37,836
Thank you as well, Mrs. Lily Torillo.

507
00:30:41,589 --> 00:30:43,174
I love you so much.

508
00:30:44,425 --> 00:30:46,386
I love you so much too, Diego.

509
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:48,930
I'll say it again.

510
00:30:49,013 --> 00:30:53,059
You are my life and my governor.

511
00:30:53,393 --> 00:30:56,312
[uplifting music playing]

512
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:04,279
[cheers and applause]

513
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:19,836
[cheers and applause continue]

514
00:31:30,305 --> 00:31:33,641
[crowd chants] Governor Diego!

515
00:31:38,980 --> 00:31:40,565
[chanting continues]

516
00:31:45,486 --> 00:31:48,740
[Marlon] Governor Diego! Governor Diego!

517
00:31:48,823 --> 00:31:51,701
[crowd continues chanting]

518
